  "body": "### Summary\nAs a member scanning my MPs, I want unread conversations to stand out from read ones. Operator feedback after a device test, 2026-11-07, milestone M4:\n- the accent dot is visible;\n- the semibold title does not set them apart enough;\n- a light accent tint on the row background is wanted.\n\n### Current\n- `Messages/MessageRowView.swift:16-41` marks an unread conversation with a semibold title and an accent dot labelled \"Non lu\".\n- There is no row background.\n- `TopicListView.swift:112` (super favourite) uses `listRowBackground(Color.orange.opacity(0.12))`. That replaces the row's own background instead of layering over it.\n\n### Legacy\n`MPListView.swift:406-483` @ 2440d79 shows a semibold title and a grey \"non lu\" capsule.\n\n### HIG\nDo not use colour alone; the dot, the bold title and the \"Non lu\" label already cover that. No HIG rule forbids a state tint, so the operator's request holds.\n\n### Proposal\n- Layer a few percent of the accent over the real row background, using one shared `RowTint` helper.\n- Reuse the same helper for the super-favourite row.\n\n```swift\n.listRowBackground(isUnread ? RowTint(strength: scheme == .dark ? 0.16 : 0.10, increased: contrast == .increased) : nil)\n// RowTint = Color(.secondarySystemGroupedBackground) (or .systemBackground for a plain list) overlaid with accent.opacity(strength [+0.08])\n```\n\nSet the list style explicitly so the base colour matches. On iPad, the tint must not hide the selection highlight.\n\n### Acceptance\n- A test of the strength rule.\n- A Mac check in light, dark, Increase Contrast, iPad selection and Dynamic Type XL.\n- A GAP row records the change.\n\nRouting: Sonnet 5.5 → Opus 5.5, effort S. Part of the visual consistency umbrella.",
